<p><em>Maple Honey on a Landes door, with Maple Natural, Maple Golden, and Maple Pebble chips for comparison.</em></p>

<h2>Where it sits in the maple stain range</h2>

<p>Set next to the existing maple stains, Maple Honey fills a gap: warmer and deeper than <strong>Natural</strong>, softer and less orange than <strong>Golden</strong>, and warmer than the gray-leaning <strong>Pebble</strong>. It's a quiet, mid-light brown that lets maple's figure show — a good answer for clients who want a wood kitchen that isn't white oak.</p>

<h2>What you need to know to order</h2>

<ul>
  <li><strong>Orderable now.</strong> Maple Honey is <strong>not yet in the spec book or 2020 Design</strong>, but it is currently available to order — add it on the order form.</li>
  <li><strong>Works with glazes and highlights.</strong> Maple Honey can be paired with glazes and highlights for a more layered or traditional look.</li>
  <li><strong>On the newest door styles.</strong> W.W. Wood is showing the new <a href="/playbook/cambridge-door-style/">Cambridge</a> door in Maple Honey.</li>
</ul>

<h2>Samples</h2>

<ul>
  <li><strong>Color chip:</strong> W.W. Wood Products is sending your showroom a Maple Honey color-chip sample <strong>at no charge</strong>.</li>
  <li><strong>Full-size door sample:</strong> fill out an <strong>Eclipse or Shiloh Standard Order Form</strong> with the sample door of your choice in Maple Honey and send it to your Pinnacle Sales rep. It ships with your <strong>showroom discount</strong> applied.</li>
</ul>

